                        


Item #:  SCP-5655

Object Class:  Euclid

Containment site lead scientist:  Dr To██ ███

Special containment procedures:  scp-5655 is to be kept in its containment cell at all times, any personnel seen trying to move scp-5655 outside of its cell will be terminated immediately. Scp-5655 is to be kept in a glass case which can be easily removed for any tests conducted on scp-5655.

Scp-5655’s containment cell is to be viewed at all times by the on-site monitoring system, only one armed personnel is required on-site at all times.

Weekly access to animal remains, D-class personnel remains if necessary, and a wide selection of bones is required.

Description:  scp-5655 is a sentient human skull made from a substance similar to that of bone. But incredibly more durable than any known earth-based material. Visually scp-5655 is an off creamy colour, with visible cracks, and only 3 teeth missing. Scp-5655 experiences a phenomenon every week on a non-specified day where it completely comes to life and interacts with objects and personnel around it. Scp-5655 claims to be able to see, hear, smell and taste, many tests have taken place to prove this, and all have been proven true.

During the phenomenon scp-5655 asks for nothing but bones and refuses to answer any questions before being provided with bones, Dr H█████ Atlis has decided bones are to be given to scp-5655 when asked, but to dispose of all bones before scp-5655's phenomenon is over. Scp-5655 is able to make any personnel bring him what he wants, it is believed scp-5655 excretes a form of hypnosis over affected personnel, it also attempts to persuade individuals itself with very unconvincing arguments, but with the hypnosis in effect scp-5655 exclusively thinks its simply very convincing. Scp-5655 speaks in a very polite tone, similar to that of a father speaking to his son. It is unknown whether this is an act or not. Personnel affected by this form of hypnosis describes scp-5655 as bright white in colour, no missing teeth, no cracks or dents, and a faint smell of lavender emanating from it.

When bones are given to scp-5655 it is able to hold and connect them together with small fleshy tendrils that extrude from the foramen magnum at the bottom of the skull. Scp-5655 is able to connect these bone pieces together and form a rudimentary skeleton, it is important to note that the origin of each bone will not affect scp-5655’s construction ability, it is able to use this skeleton to become mobile, but Dr H█████ Atlis has limited the amount of time scp-5655 is able to use the bones to five minutes, as not to give a feeling of freedom, one the bones are removed from scp-5655’s cell it begins to shout profanities at personnel until the phenomenon is over.

When scp-5655 is dormant, personnel continuously report that scp-5655 is watching them, or that they see it blink, when in a dormant state scp-5655 is to be considered hostile, as scp-5655 is only harmless during its once a week phenomenon. Many personnel are effected by scp-5655’s hypnosis in its supposed dormant state, but only a few are spoken to by it, when being spoken to by scp-5655 personnel report being asked about themselves, and eventually being asked to give their skin and flesh to scp-5655, personnel affected by this begin ripping off their own skin and flesh and will only be stopped by being completely restrained, while being questioned about this, affected personnel describes scp-5655 being in disarray, with teeth missing, holes and cracks everywhere, with the skull almost being completely black in colouring, the bone-like texture now being similar to that of rusted metal, rotting flesh is also smelled by the affected personnel, and doesn't become weaker or stronger if moving. The voice being heard is described as if it came from a faraway siren, and not directly from scp-5655 itself.

Additional notes:  Scp-5655 was put into foundation containment on 17/6/20██ it was found in the small town of ██████, Alaska, local police reports tell of disturbing sights In an abandoned construction site on the south side of town, with residents finding large mounds of flesh and bone all surrounding a single skull in the center of the mass.

Agents arrived and retrieved scp-5655 from the construction site with no resistance

Scp-5655 has been moved to a US site in Dallas Texas, site-██ as a part of a new facility centered around scp-xxxx(my first scp).

